A||N||5||sparks||clutch cylinder?||||5||
Z||000000||sparks||10-16-2000||10:15 AM||||Hi, I just bought an 85 Fiero, at least I think it's an 85.  The guy selling it says it's an 88 but I know enough to know it's not an 88.<P>Anyway it's a 2.5L.  When you first get in if you pump the clutch 2-3 times it'll shift fine.  But if you don't it won't shift correctly.  The seller really didn't know much about it mechanically or otherwise and pointed at what I would call the clutch cylinder and said "that pump there needs to be replaced and it'll fix it".<P>Sounds right to me w/ my experiences in my Jeeps.  It just had a new clutch put in 600 miles ago.<P>So is this what it needs?  And what exactly is the part I'm needing to buy to fix it and how do I fix it?<P>Thanks,<BR><P>------------------<BR>--<BR>sparks||||reg||5
Z||000001||polomeno||10-16-2000||10:54 AM||||Sounds to me like a leaky clutch .. could be either the clutch master or slave cylinder ..or the line.. with mine it was the master cylinder right where it connect with your clutch pedal.. so give that a check and see what it looks like.. i replaced both and it worked just fine..<P>John<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||sparks||10-16-2000||11:12 AM||||Where's the best place to get them?<P>Price and difficulty in replacing?<P>Oh, is the slave cylinder internal or external?  External I hope???<BR><P>------------------<BR>--<BR>sparks||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||10-16-2000||11:38 AM||||The slave is external.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||10-16-2000||04:50 PM||||The best place to get clutch slave and master cylinders is your local Pontiac dealer.  It will cost more than a parts store, but you will not have any problems with your hydraulics for many, many years and many, many miles.<P>The aftermarket hydraulics (Bendix, Wagner, Raybestos, etc.) are all made by the same company and are prone to leaks and quality issues.<P>As for whether or not it is an '85 or an '88.....look at the VIN#.  The 10th digit is the year code......"J" is '88 and "F" is '85.  <p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 10-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||sparks||10-17-2000||07:44 AM||||Thanks for the info on where to get the parts.<P>I was right.  It's an 85.  I picked it up last nite, the title said 85 on it.  I didn't bother pointing it out to the seller...<P>Drove it 1.5 hours home w/ no problems.  Engine light came on once breifly then went off.<P>Just needs a little bit of cleaning up and should be in good shape.  I was pretty happy with how solid it is for it's age.  Someone has taken good care of it!<P>------------------<BR>--<BR>sparks||||reg||1
